  "issue_number": 15496,
  "issue_title": "looseEqual: comparing Map/Set values with circular references throws RangeError (regression in 3.5.42)",
  "issue_body": "### Vue version\n3.5.42 (also reproduced on current `main`, commit `5409708`)\n\n### Link to minimal reproduction\nhttps://play.vuejs.org/#eyJBcHAudnVlIjogIjxzY3JpcHQgc2V0dXA-XG5pbXBvcnQgeyByZWYgfSBmcm9tICd2dWUnXG5cbmNvbnN0IG1ha2VHcmFwaCA9ICgpID0--XG4gIDxzZWxlY3Qgdi1tb2RlbD1cInNlbGVjdGVkXCI-XG4gICAgPG9wdGlvbiA6dmFsdWU9XCJvcHRBXCI-QTwvb3B0aW9uPlxuICAgIDxvcHRpb24gOnZhbHVlPVwib3B0QlwiPkI8L29wdGlvbj5cbiAgPC9zZWxlY3Q-XG48L3RlbXBsYXRlPlxuIiwgImltcG9ydC1tYXAuanNvbiI6ICJ7XCJpbXBvcnRzXCI6IHtcInZ1ZVwiOiBcImh0dHBzOi8vdW5wa2cuY29tL0B2dWUvcnVudGltZS1kb21AMy41LjQyL2Rpc3QvcnVudGltZS1kb20uZXNtLWJyb3dzZXIuanNcIn19In0=\n\n### Steps to reproduce\nOpen the reproduction above: a `<select v-model>` whose option `:value`s are `Set`s containing mutually-referencing objects. The component throws during mount, before any interaction.\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\n\nconst makeGraph = () => {\n  const n1 = { id: 1 }\n  const n2 = { id: 2 }\n  n1.peer = n2\n  n2.peer = n1  // circular reference\n  return new Set([n1, n2])\n}\n\nconst optA = makeGraph()\nconst optB = makeGraph()\nconst selected = ref(optB)\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <select v-model=\"selected\">\n    <option :value=\"optA\">A</option>\n    <option :value=\"optB\">B</option>\n  </select>\n</template>\n```\n\n### What is expected?\nMounting the select should not throw. `looseEqual` should safely terminate on cyclic structures (e.g. by tracking already-visited pairs) and return `true` for two structurally identical cyclic Sets/Maps.\n\n### What is actually happening?\nMounting throws `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded`:\n\n```\nRangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded\n    at looseCompareCollections (packages/shared/src/looseEqual.ts:16)\n    at looseEqual (packages/shared/src/looseEqual.ts:64)\n    at looseCompareCollections (packages/shared/src/looseEqual.ts:22)\n    at looseEqual (packages/shared/src/looseEqual.ts:64)\n    ...\n[Vue warn]: Unhandled error during execution of directive hook\n```\n\n### System Info\nReproduced locally with `vuejs/core@main` (5409708) via vitest: both the unit-level `looseEqual` calls and the component-level render path (same shape as the test added in #15328) throw `RangeError`.\n\n### Any additional comments?\nThis is a **regression introduced by #15328** (\"fix(shared): correctly compare Map and Set values\", released in **v3.5.42**), which added `looseCompareCollections` in `packages/shared/src/looseEqual.ts`:\n\n```ts\nfunction looseCompareCollections(\n  a: Map<any, any> | Set<any>,\n  b: Map<any, any> | Set<any>,\n) {\n  if (a.size !== b.size) return false\n  const candidates = Array.from(b)\n  const matched = new Uint8Array(candidates.length)\n  for (const item of a) {\n    let index = -1\n    for (let i = 0; i < candidates.length; i++) {\n      if (!matched[i] && looseEqual(item, candidates[i])) {\n        index = i\n        break\n      }\n    }\n    if (index < 0) return false\n    matched[index] = 1\n  }\n  return true\n}\n```\n\n`looseEqual(item, candidates[i])` recurses into each `[key, value]` pair (Map) or element (Set), so a Map/Set whose entries point back to the collection itself or to each other causes unbounded recursion. Before 3.5.42, Maps/Sets never recursed into their entries (they fell through to `String()` comparison), so this exact code path \u2014 a `<select v-model>` with Map/Set values, which is precisely the scenario #15320/#15328 added support for \u2014 **did not throw on 3.5.41**; it silently compared wrong, which #15328 fixed.\n\nNote: #5318 covers the same root cause for cyclic plain objects (pre-existing, still open). The Map/Set case is new in 3.5.42: cyclic Maps/Sets did not throw before.\n\nSuggested fix: make `looseEqual` cycle-safe by tracking visited `(a, b)` pairs (e.g. with a `WeakMap<object, Set<object>>` and returning `true` on re-encounter), which also fixes #5318.\n\nAdditional local repro cases that all throw `RangeError` on current main:\n- `looseEqual(new Set([a1, a2]), new Set([b1, b2]))` where `a1.peer = a2; a2.peer = a1` and `b1.peer = b2; b2.peer = b1`\n- `looseEqual(mapA, mapB)` where both maps hold mutually-referencing values\n- `looseEqual(s1, s2)` where `s1.add(s1)` and `s2.add(s2)`\n",
